=== task: mcq medium
title: Build once, ask many times
prompt: A list holds n names, and a program must answer q questions of the form "is this name in the list?". It turns the list into a set first. What is the total cost?
* O(n + q): O(n) to build the set, then O(1) for each question :: Right.
- O(n × q): each question searches the list :: That's the cost without the set.
- O(q): the set answers each question in O(1) :: Building the set takes O(n) first.
- O(n log n + q): the set has to be sorted :: A set isn't sorted; `set(names)` is built in O(n).
hint: What does `set(names)` cost?
hint: And each question afterwards?
right: Build once, ask many times: O(n + q). For n = q = 10,000, that's about 20,000 steps instead of 100,000,000.
wrong: `set(names)` is O(n). Each `in` on the set is O(1), so q questions are O(q). Together: O(n + q).

