fail[6]: 1 → 5 and 5 → 9. The two 5s are one value.
hint: Use the set `values`, so that each value is counted once.
hint: For each value a, there's a pair if `a + k` is in the set.
hint: Count those values.
right: Each value needs one O(1) check for its partner: O(n). Checking every pair of values would be O(n²).
wrong: Make a set of the values. For each value a, check whether a + k is also in the set, and count how many times it is.

